Z||000000||88 Fiero||09-28-1999||11:47 PM||||Hey guys!!!! I was cruising the web when I ran into this guys info on his fiero. He got 130K miles on his car and with a few simple bolt ons he got some good extra horses... This is the address of his results in his Fiero...Tell me what you think??? I think it's neat to see a Fiero that can generate that much horse power with over 100k miles on it...http://thefieroclub.com/osg/dyno.htm ||||reg||10
Z||000001||GT Bastard||09-29-1999||01:02 AM||||I hate to be negative, but those Dyno runs are pretty discouraging.  In fact, they suck...  I realize the engine has a few miles on it, but the guy has some decent mods and his hp and torque are still pretty lame.  Lets face it, the Fiero v6's weren't built to be powerhouses, but they're fun cars to drive and they handle like a "raped-ape."<BR>Just my opinion....<BR>-later||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||09-29-1999||06:43 AM||||Bear in mind that dyno horsepower numbers are rear-wheel values. This means that they will be substantially lower (10-20 percent) than crankshaft power levels.  If one knows how to interpret these fiqures, they are not "bad" results at all.<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||88 Fiero||09-29-1999||10:07 AM||||I agree with you MW...I think for basically I should say bone stock engine with headers and 130K miles that's pretty good HP gains...||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||09-29-1999||12:20 PM||||I understand what rear-wheel horsepower is, but I still think the car is underpowered... BWAHAHAHAHAHAHAAHH!!!!!BWAHAHAHAHHAHHAHAH!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!  But again, it's still a blast to drive.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mwbackus||09-29-1999||05:51 PM||||Well GTB, considering the fact that you have a stock automatic, and it is obviously in pretty bad condition (assuming some of your other posts are factual) I guess one could say that "your particluar" car probably IS underpowered..<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||09-30-1999||11:59 AM||||Well, MW.... The engine is actually in prime shape.  It idles a little rough until it warms up, but it runs very smooth and doesn't smoke or burn oil.  The rest of the car is what needs the work, and most of it is already done.  All that's left is the aesthethics(sp?).  At any rate, even the best running GT out there isn't impressive on the 1/4 mile or dyno.  Lets face it, 140 hp from 6 cylinders is just a little on the wimpy side of things.  Wouldn't you agree?  I'm not trying to be an ass, I'm just stating the obvious guys!<P>later,<BR>Jeff||||reg||1
Z||000007||88 Fiero||09-30-1999||12:40 PM||||GT...I disagree with you.. first of all the question is...do you have an automatic or a stick shift?? if you have an automatic then you will be behind in some other peoples car when you race unless your going to run some nitrous or engine modified. A stick shift fiero V6 makes alot of difference. Your wondering why I know that...Been involve with Fiero's since '85 and an FOCOA member since that year. I've seen this cars tested in a race auto's and sticks. I've race an '88 Camaro RS V8 (a friend of mine) against my '85 GT with a 4-speed and beat him. He was at the back end of my door. We tried again and race longer than a 1/4 mile to see how far my car can go... Well I ran out of gears and he beat me...and my car at that time got 97,000 miles on it. So unless your car is automatic then that's something to be considered as slow as what you prefferbly to think...||||reg||1
Z||000008||mwbackus||09-30-1999||01:18 PM||||I doubt many of those who post on this forum are still in this "140" hp range.  It is all too easy and cost effective to improve this number significantly.  Your critique of someones efforts to improve their cars performance was not well taken by me.  My 500 hp Mitsubishi 3000GT VR4 would easily blow the doors off of anything you own, but it certainly does not warrant an attitude like you have.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000009||Greg Piet||09-30-1999||04:45 PM||||Well under my decklid my car is entirely stock as of present (except the dogbone), and to be honest I can smoke many many cars out there on these little sprints.  I do however know better than to think about going against a vette, or other obviously superior machines (like a 500hp 3000GT).  All my friends that know anthing about cars are impressed with the little plastic car that could, and dont see a point in me wanting to make it go faster.  "that this is already really quick, why the H*ll do you want it any faster?" is a common comment.<BR>I think most of the "bragging" done here is because people here love their fieros, and this is a venue where they are likely not going to be laughed at, or have to defend their cars that seem to always get picked on in the company of V8 owners.<BR>Cant we all just get along??||||reg||1
Z||000010||GT Bastard||09-30-1999||04:59 PM||||Dear MWbackus,<P>In your last post, you stated: "My 500 hp Mitsubishi 3000GT VR4 would easily blow the doors off of anything you own, but it certainly does not warrant an attitude like you have."  The fact that you said this and told ME that I have an ATTITIDE in the same sentence is just a little hypocritical.  Furthermore, how can you know what cars I own?  And better yet, WHY DOES IT MATTER!?  Your response to my post was totally off the subject.  I apologize if I sounded like I had an attitude, but I'm not trying to start a war.  For your information, I also own a '94 Z28 Camaro, and yes, I'm sure that you and your insanely expensive Mitsubishi could beat my poor white-trash Z28.  Is that what you wanted?  All I wanted to do was voice my opinion!  Let me try to state it in more clear-cut terms: I think Fiero's kick ass, and that's why I bought one.  All I'm saying is, 140hp seems a little meager for a V6, BUT THAT'S OK!!!!!!  I just wanted to see if anybody felt the same way I do.   Sorry for any emotional stress I may have caused anyone.   <P>later fella's,<BR>-Jeff<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Patrick||09-30-1999||05:37 PM||||<BR>.... meanwhile, those of us with the 4-bangers are off in the corner whimpering...<P>||||reg||9
Z||000012||four50four||09-30-1999||05:42 PM||||MW, Greendano has a pro-street ranger with a 460 in it, that probably produces close to that HP, but with much more torque. I'd say in a straight line, the ranger would win. don't say that your mitisbishi would smoke it in the corners, because this wasn't made to go fast in corners. fast can mean a lot of different things to different people.  such as i bet my 1977 chevrolet jimmy is way faster than your mitisbishi, off-road that is. we've never had problems with flame wars before, so lets everybody try to keep the piece. now, lets see some smiliys!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by four50four (edited 09-30-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||mwbackus||09-30-1999||06:19 PM||||There will always be a car faster and better than what you or I may have, thats a fact of life.  I do not compare my fiero to my mitsubishi, that would be silly.  The point I was making is the other cars you may own that may be superior in some ways, does not justify trashing ones attempt to increase the performance of his ride.  If you are not satisfied with the horsepower of your particular Fiero, then put your money where you mouth is and do something about it, rather then trashing the dyno results of someone that is at least doing something more than just talk.<P>BTW, the site referenced in the original post no longer exists.  Is it real hard to understand that with over 450 members, the proud owner of those dyno results, may have been reading these discussions? <P>Mike<P><p>[This message has been edited by mwbackus (edited 09-30-1999).]||||reg||1
